DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("(x/10)*5");
$fun_1 = Formula("((x)^(1/2))*4");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("{-8, 0, 7} U [1, 12]");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("({-8, 0, 7} - {-8, 0, 7})");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("(-infinity, 10) U (-infinity, 10)");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("({-10, 1} U (-infinity, 10) U {-10, 1} - ((-infinity, infinity) - ((-infinity, 10)))) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (-infinity, 10)) U ((-infinity, 10) U {-10, 1} - ((-infinity, infinity) - (-infinity, 10)))");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

[`0/8+6/14`] is equal to [_____]{Formula('0.428571428571')}
---

What is the value of [`19+3+17`]? [_____]{answer=>39,width=>10}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x < 10\}`]
- [`B = \{-10, 1\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`(B \cup A \cup B \cap (A)) \cap A \cup (A \cup B \cap A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | 1 \leq x \leq 12\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x < 18\}`]
- [`C = \{-8, 0, 7\}`]

Compute:
- [`C \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`C - C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -10, 10, -9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -5, 3, -4 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-5, 3, -4>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-10, 10, -9>") x Compute("<-5, 3, -4>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-10, 10, -9>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, 3, -4>") x Compute("<-10, 10, -9>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-10, 10, -9>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, 3, -4>") . Compute("<-10, 10, -9>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -6, 10, 8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 5, -1, 4 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<5, -1, 4>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-6, 10, 8>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<5, -1, 4>") x Compute("<-6, 10, 8>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-6, 10, 8>"))}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(8) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>8)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
